Section name: Conclusion
Excerpt:
This paper presented algorithms that significantly improve inference time and memory efficiency for quantized neu- ral networks (like LLMs) with binary and ternary weights. By preprocessing weight matrices to create indices, our approach reduces storage complexity for maintaining the model weights by a logarithmic factor. It enhances inference efficiency, achieving a time complexity of O(n2 logn). Furthermore, our experiment results across various settings demonstrated the practical advantages of our methods, with observed reductions in inference time of up to 29x and memory usage of up to 6x. 10PyTorch default settings such as caching mechanisms, backend-specific optimizations (e.g., cuBLAS, cuDNN), and ker- nel fusion, are fully enabled. 8 An Efficient Matrix Multiplication Algorithm for Accelerating Inference in Binary and Ternary Neural Networks

